---
import Default from "../../layouts/Default.astro";
import {LogoHistory} from "../../data/scripts/database";
import Alert from "../../components/Alert.astro";
import Card from "../../components/Card.astro";
---
<Default title="About us" description="You want to know who we are? Find out here!" banner={true}>
<section class="text-left">
<h2>Company polices</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="/about/polices/terms-of-service">Terms of service</a></li>
<li><a href="/about/polices/other-information">Unrelated, but important information</a></li>
<li><a href="/about/polices/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a></li>
</ul>
</section>
<br />
<section class="text-left">
<h2>Introduction</h2>
<Alert type="info">
<p>This section is under construction! Check back later when we update it!</p>
</Alert>
</section>
<br />
<section class="text-left">
<h2>Logo evolution</h2>
<p>The history of our somewhat interesting logo</p>
<div class="grid-small">
{LogoHistory.flatMap((item) => (
<Card title={item.title} icon={null} link={null}>
<h2>What it looks like</h2>
<img src={item.image} style="width: 64px;" alt={`logo${item.id}`} />
<h2>Timeline</h2>
<ul class="list-none p-0">
<li>Created since: {item.started_on}</li>
<li>Been used until: {item.until_now}</li>
</ul>
</Card>
))}
</div>
</section>
<br />
<section class="text-left">
<h2>Donate</h2>
<p>Your generous donation helps us out greatly and keeps us alive for years to come!</p>
<Alert type="info">We have our own payment processing subdomain, which will cover all transactions that you make using Stripe. For more information on how this works, please refer to the Stripe documentation website for more information!</Alert>
<section class="text-left">
<h2>Why support us</h2>
<p>Supporting our work that we create and share helps us out in expanding our infrastructure, adding more services, expanding our workload, and to keep us alive for years to come. Any donation, whenever it be small or large, will tell us that you love our work and that you are willing to be a part of our team. Your support helps cover server costs, domain fees, and dedicated time for updates and bug fixes.</p>
</section>
<br />
<section class="text-left">
<h2>How to Donate</h2>
<p>
Set up your recurring donation using <a href="https://liberapay.com/">Liberapay</a>. The platform allows the use of the <a href="https://stripe.com">Stripe eConverse</a> platform in order to process all payment information securely, and effectively. Our profile link will be located in the footer below. Currently, we don't offer any other platforms that you can use to send us your donation. For now, we recommend that you use our preferred platform above if you want to send us your donation more easier.
<br />
If you want to have an account in order to manage all of your donations more easily, check out our <a href="https://pay.ttnrtsite.me">payment processing dashboard</a> to find out more on how you can do that! Note that their may be some changes in the near future, as we are very much new to this whole "stripe" thing anyway. Please bear with us as we try to sort some stuff out!
</p>
</section>
<br />
<section class="text-left">
<h2>What you should expect</h2>
<ul>
<li>The entire payment process is governed under Stripe's terms and conditions agreement, meaning that whatever purchase that you make using their platform will be fully secure and private from anyone that is trying to get any information about your transaction.</li>
<li>We will <strong>never sell or give out</strong> any transactions that you make, even if it is just for fun or for the use of jokes. Refunds are provided by their policy agreements, though you should consider contacting our support team if you would like to refund the donation that you made.</li>
<li>Additionally, some countries that have their own money currency might not be allowed to donate to us. This is protect our company and to safe guard our users when they are making any purchases that go through our Stripe account.</li>
<li>You need to be at least <strong>13 years old or older</strong> in order to donate using <a href="https://liberapay.com/">Liberapay</a>. This is in corrdination with our <strong>Terms of Use agreement</strong> and with <strong>Liberapay's Terms of Use agreement</strong> as well!</li>
</ul>
</section>
</section>
</Default>